<p>A Qatari helicopter crashed in the state&#x27;s regional waters after a technical malfunction, Qatar&#x27;s Defence Ministry said. Officials said search-and-rescue operations were under way for the crew and passengers.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ZYqanZZrc1InUnpAIcYm0S8CKkD_58BYUz2DijPLmswT3tPsFt_nOWvQkfZlyS8n7z1MCfWRiVuHlw1-uFF6QAs--7gM0twtVdnSSv0vjaWO' alt='People sit with the reflection of the Doha skyline along the Doha Corniche, on the second day of Eidul Fitr in Doha on March 21, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Key details remain unclear: Qatar had not said where the helicopter was headed, the exact crash site, or how many people were on board at the time of the reports.</li><li>Available reports identified the aircraft as a Qatari military helicopter.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Qatar Defence Ministry: The ministry said the helicopter was carrying out routine duty when it crashed, offering its official account of the flight&#x27;s purpose. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/qatar-military-helicopter-crashed-in-the-gulf/article70771421.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Qatar Interior Ministry: The ministry focused on the response, saying several specialized teams had been deployed to support the search. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1984283/helicopter-crashes-in-qatar-after-technical-malfunction-during-routine-duty-ministry'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Dawn reporting: The report said Qatar has faced several strikes since the start of the Middle East war, but added that no link had been made between those events and this crash. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1984283/helicopter-crashes-in-qatar-after-technical-malfunction-during-routine-duty-ministry'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/qatar-military-helicopter-crashed-in-the-gulf/article70771421.ece'>Qatar helicopter crashes after &#x27;technical malfunction&#x27;: Ministry</a> - thehindu.com</li><li>